      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not provide a definition of “tropism,” nor does it explicitly support the claim that tropism is “the tendency of a virus vector to preferentially target and enter particular cell types or tissues.”",
        "The packet uses “improved tropism” in the context of rAAV capsid mutants targeting retinal vascular endothelial cells, but it does not define tropism as a general behavioral property of vectors or specify “preferentially target and enter” as the meaning.",
        "The definition’s phrasing that improved endothelial tropism means the vector “more effectively reaches and transduces vascular endothelial cells” is an interpretive paraphrase; the packet mentions improved endothelial targeting and improved transduction, but it does not explicitly equate this to the exact wording of the definition."
